## Summary

I implemented the tenure requirement for membership level 4 in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`).

**The change:** The three creation-time factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes) are still capped at 3. Level 4 is now granted only when the owner's **tenure — whole days from `registrationDate` to today — exceeds 365**:

```java
level = Math.min(level, 3);
boolean longTenure = this.registrationDate != null
    && java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365;
if (longTenure) {
    level++;
}
return level;
```

**Why a new owner never exceeds level 3:** a newly created owner registers today, so its tenure is 0 days (not > 365), and the tenure step never fires. A new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, and a 3-member household maxes the pre-tenure factors at 3 and stays there — exactly as `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts.

I also updated the method's Javadoc to describe the 1–4 range and the tenure rule, and mirrored the existing `getAgeBand()` pattern by null-guarding `registrationDate`.

